# EtAssetItem

## Purpose

Tailored, asset-focused list item for the eToro design system. Built with a compound component pattern so consumers compose a row from opinionated subcomponents (`Logo`, `Content`, `Symbol`, `Name`, `Label`, `Price`, `Change`, `Trailing`, `RateChip`, `Divider`, `Skeleton`) instead of passing a large, structured props blob.

Unlike the generic `EtListItemV2` (which supports both assets and people via free-form slots), `EtAssetItem` is intentionally narrow: it knows about logos, symbols, names, prices, changes, and labels, and renders them with the design-system styling that asset rows require. Consumers cannot drift from the design system because the API does not expose primitives that would let them.

For people/user rows, build a separate `EtUserItem` component with its own opinionated subcomponents — do not extend `EtAssetItem`.

For swipe-to-reveal actions, wrap `EtAssetItem` with `EtSwipeableRow` (see below).

## Architecture

```text
et-asset-item.tsx (root) → provides AssetItemContext, two render paths (skeleton / standard) × two layouts (default / trading-view)
├── EtAssetItem.Logo      → square instrument EtAvatar; size derived from context; optional fallback / market dot
├── EtAssetItem.Content   → vertical container for Symbol/Name (flex: 1)
├── EtAssetItem.Symbol    → primary line (semibold, ellipsized)
├── EtAssetItem.Name      → secondary line (tertiary text, ellipsized)
├── EtAssetItem.Label     → opinionated middle-slot pill (wraps EtBadge size="small")
├── EtAssetItem.Price     → right-aligned, pre-formatted price string (default layout only)
├── EtAssetItem.Change    → pre-formatted change string with sentiment-driven color; right-aligned in default, left-aligned + smaller under Symbol in trading-view
├── EtAssetItem.Trailing  → arbitrary right-side slot (default layout only; replaces legacy rightElement)
├── EtAssetItem.RateChip  → display-only sentiment-colored pill, rendered as a horizontal row (trading-view only)
├── EtAssetItem.Divider   → hairline separator below the row
└── EtAssetItem.Skeleton  → loading placeholder shaped like a real asset row (variants: 2-lines, symbol-only, rate-chips)

EtSwipeableRow (public, standalone) → wraps EtAssetItem to add swipe-to-reveal actions
└── EtSwipeableRow.Action → action button subcomponents revealed on left swipe
```

